  "per-column-type-fidelity-real-sql-types-over-the-wire": {
    "section": "Data Warehouse (`data-warehouse/`)",
    "claim": "Per-column type fidelity (real SQL types over the wire)",
    "witnesses": [
      "go:TestResultTypeFidelity",
      "go:TestReflectDecimalColumn",
      "go:TestReflectedSQLTypesMatchFabric",
      "go:TestNestedColumnsAreOmittedNotFabricated",
      "go:TestNestedColumnsStayOmittedThroughTheDeltaRoute",
      "go:TestNestedOmissionSurvivesSchemaEvolutionOrder",
      "go:TestNumericWidthsMatchFabric",
      "go:TestDeltaStringReflectsAsVarchar",
      "ci:medallion"
    ],
    "note": "The Go witnesses prove the MAP (a Parquet column of each logical type reflects to the right SQL type). ci:medallion proves the ROUTE: e2e/type-map/probe.py writes the types from Spark and reads INFORMATION_SCHEMA back over ODBC, which no Go test can cover because neither end of that seam is Go. The two DeltaRoute/SchemaEvolution witnesses exist because a map-only assertion missed a real defect: v0.16.0 omitted nested columns in the reader and then re-added them as NULL in the projection, and the map test asserted one stage too early to see it."
  },
